    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0699" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 103.94/416</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-13T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 13, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.45 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1853. To Baruch from Summers:</p>
                <p>Maritime Council requires by September 20:</p>
                <p>Approximate statement of amounts necessary to import, year commencing September
                    1, 1918, ending August 31, 1919. Also what, if any, shipping arranged for. State
                    consumption imports and exports, also stocks on hand, if possible, of each fiber
                    for year ending September 1, 1918, and ports of origin of imports for jute,
                    flax, hemp, sisal and similar fibers.</p>
                <p>An immediate answer imperative. Patterson.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
